@page "/"
@layout Layout.LandingLayout
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>LocalGhost · GitHub to IIS, clearly</PageTitle>

<div class="landing">
    <div class="landing-glow"></div>
    <header class="landing-nav landing-wrap">
        <a class="landing-brand" href="/" aria-label="LocalGhost home"><span class="brand-mark"><img src="/localghost-logo-transparent.png" alt="" width="31" height="31" /></span><span>LocalGhost<small>SELF-HOSTED CI/CD</small></span></a>
        <nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a><a href="#supported">What it supports</a></nav>
        <div class="landing-nav-actions"><a class="nav-signin" href="/login">Sign in</a><a class="nav-register" href="/register">Create account <span>↗</span></a></div>
    </header>

    <main>
        <section class="landing-hero landing-wrap">
            <div class="hero-copy">
                <span class="hero-eyebrow"><i></i> BUILT FOR YOUR WINDOWS + IIS SERVER</span>
                <h1>Deploy from GitHub.<br /><em>See every step.</em></h1>
                <p>LocalGhost pairs a background worker service with a detailed web dashboard. The worker watches your chosen branches, builds your app, and deploys it to IIS; the dashboard lets you follow live output, inspect past runs, and manage every project.</p>
                <div class="hero-actions"><a class="primary-action" href="/register">Create your account <span>→</span></a><a class="secondary-action" href="/login">I already have an account</a></div>
                <div class="hero-footnote"><span>✦</span> Your projects start in your own workspace. Add a repository when you’re ready.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-preview" aria-label="Example deployment pipeline">
                <div class="preview-top"><div><span class="preview-symbol">◆</span><span><strong>Project pipeline</strong><small>From commit to IIS</small></span></div><span class="preview-live"><i></i> LIVE VIEW</span></div>
                <div class="preview-steps">
                    <div><span class="step-number">01</span><span class="step-icon source">⑂</span><span><strong>Source</strong><small>GitHub branch</small></span><b>✓</b></div>
                    <div><span class="step-number">02</span><span class="step-icon build">⌘</span><span><strong>Build</strong><small>.NET / React</small></span><b>✓</b></div>
                    <div><span class="step-number">03</span><span class="step-icon deploy">◈</span><span><strong>Deploy</strong><small>IIS site</small></span><b>✓</b></div>
                    <div><span class="step-number">04</span><span class="step-icon verify">✓</span><span><strong>Verify</strong><small>App pool / health URL</small></span><b>✓</b></div>
                </div>
                <div class="preview-log"><div class="log-heading"><span><i></i><i></i><i></i></span> deployment.log</div><p><time>14:07:12</time><span class="log-green">✓</span> Source synchronized</p><p><time>14:07:31</time><span class="log-green">✓</span> Build completed</p><p><time>14:07:35</time><span class="log-green">✓</span> Backup created</p><p><time>14:07:39</time><span class="log-violet">●</span> Site is live on IIS</p></div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="landing-strip landing-wrap" aria-label="Key capabilities"><span><b>01</b> Background worker service</span><span><b>02</b> Detailed live dashboard</span><span><b>03</b> Backup &amp; rollback</span><span><b>04</b> Branch monitoring</span></section>

        <section id="how-it-works" class="landing-section landing-wrap">
            <div class="section-intro"><span class="section-kicker">THE WORKFLOW</span><h2>From commit to running site.</h2><p>A practical pipeline that stays visible from source checkout through verification.</p></div>
            <div class="workflow-grid">
                <article><span class="workflow-icon">⑂</span><small>01 / CONNECT</small><h3>Choose your repository</h3><p>Connect GitHub or use a personal access token. Select the branches this project should watch.</p></article>
                <article><span class="workflow-icon">⌘</span><small>02 / BUILD</small><h3>Publish your app</h3><p>LocalGhost checks out the commit and runs the configured .NET publish and optional React build.</p></article>
                <article><span class="workflow-icon">◈</span><small>03 / DEPLOY</small><h3>Move safely to IIS</h3><p>It backs up the current site, deploys the published files, and can roll back when deployment fails.</p></article>
                <article><span class="workflow-icon">✓</span><small>04 / OBSERVE</small><h3>Know what happened</h3><p>Follow live steps, review run history, and optionally check an HTTP health endpoint.</p></article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="supported" class="landing-section support-section landing-wrap">
            <div class="section-intro"><span class="section-kicker">SUPPORTED TODAY</span><h2>Made for the apps you run on IIS.</h2><p>Start with the deployment types the agent can build and publish now.</p></div>
            <div class="support-grid">
                <article><span class="support-icon violet">◎</span><div><h3>Blazor Web App</h3><p>Publish the server project and deploy it as one ASP.NET Core IIS site.</p></div><span class="support-tag">.NET</span></article>
                <article><span class="support-icon cyan">⌘</span><div><h3>ASP.NET Core API</h3><p>Publish a Web API project directly to its IIS site.</p></div><span class="support-tag">.NET</span></article>
                <article><span class="support-icon amber">✳</span><div><h3>API + React</h3><p>Publish the API and build a separate React frontend for IIS.</p></div><span class="support-tag">.NET + NODE</span></article>
            </div>
            <div class="coming-soon"><div><span class="section-kicker">COMING SOON</span><h3>More ways to deploy.</h3><p>These deployment templates are planned, not available in the current agent.</p></div><div class="coming-soon-list"><span>MERN</span><span>Next.js</span><span>ASP.NET MVC</span><span>ABP.io</span></div></div>
        </section>

        <section class="landing-cta landing-wrap"><div><span class="section-kicker">READY WHEN YOU ARE</span><h2>Make your next deployment a clear one.</h2><p>Create an account, add your first project, and keep the full journey in view.</p></div><a class="primary-action" href="/register">Get started <span>→</span></a></section>
    </main>

    <footer class="landing-footer landing-wrap"><span><img src="/localghost-logo-transparent.png" alt="" width="20" height="20" /> LocalGhost</span><span>Self-hosted GitHub → IIS deployment</span><a href="/login">Sign in</a></footer>
</div>

